.TH "bup\-server" "1" "2026\-09\-01" "Bup 0.34" ""
.SH NAME
bup\-server \- the server side of the bup client\-server relationship
.SH SYNOPSIS
bup server
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]bup server\f[R] is the server side of a remote bup session.
If you use \f[CR]bup\-split\f[R](1) or \f[CR]bup\-save\f[R](1) with the
\f[CR]\-r\f[R] option, they will ssh to the remote server and run
\f[CR]bup server\f[R] to receive the transmitted objects.
.PP
There is normally no reason to run \f[CR]bup server\f[R] yourself.
.PP
The server\[cq]s resource usage can be limited by setting
\f[CR]bup.server.deduplicate\-writes\f[R] to \f[CR]false\f[R].
See the description in \f[CR]bup\-config(5)\f[R] for additional
information.
.SH FILES
.TP
$BUP_DIR/bup\-dumb\-server
When this file exists, \f[CR]bup\f[R] will act as if
\f[CR]bup.server.deduplicate\-writes\f[R] is set to \f[CR]false\f[R] in
the configuration, unless the configuration already specifies a value.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]bup\-save\f[R](1), \f[CR]bup\-split\f[R](1),
\f[CR]bup\-config\f[R](1)
.SH BUP
Part of the \f[CR]bup\f[R](1) suite.
